WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.957
Laparoscopy means looking inside the abdomen.

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:12.434
A camera and long, slim instruments let doctors examine and treat the abdomen through small openings.

00:00:13.137 --> 00:00:16.656
The camera shows what is happening inside the body on a screen.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.067
The upper abdomen contains the liver and stomach.

00:00:21.707 --> 00:00:26.332
Lower down are the loops of the small intestine, surrounded by the large intestine.

00:00:26.914 --> 00:00:29.155
The abdominal wall protects these organs.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:33.599
A camera reveals this normally hidden working space.

00:00:34.258 --> 00:00:39.340
In many laparoscopic procedures, carbon dioxide is introduced into the abdomen.

00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:42.790
This lifts the abdominal wall away from the organs.

00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:46.352
It creates room for the camera and instruments.

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:52.925
Short access sleeves, called trocars, guide instruments through the abdominal wall.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.857
Light and a camera provide the view.

00:00:56.491 --> 00:01:02.276
The surgical team controls the instruments from outside and watches their tips on the screen.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.666
This allows gentle tissue handling and precise movements.

00:01:08.256 --> 00:01:11.866
Coordination between eyes and hands is essential.

00:01:12.499 --> 00:01:14.575
The entry point acts as a pivot.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:19.576
When the handle moves left, the instrument tip swings right.

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.817
This unfamiliar behaviour takes practice.

00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:28.610
Small, steady movements help guide the tip to its target.

00:01:29.279 --> 00:01:33.183
In our training box, a smartphone provides the camera view.

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:38.346
You watch the working area and move small rings with graspers.

00:01:38.879 --> 00:01:44.661
You practise orientation, hand-eye coordination and precise movement.

00:01:45.298 --> 00:01:51.300
The box teaches the basic principle of laparoscopy without recreating a real operation.
